  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "Two positive numbers \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) are in the ratio \\(a:b,\\) where \\(0\\lt a\\lt b.\\) If \\(x+y=c,\\) then the smaller of \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) is",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{ac}{b}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{bc-ac}{b}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{ac}{a+b}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{bc}{a+b}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{ac}{b-a}\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "c",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1982-p5.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Write \\(x=ka\\) and \\(y=kb.\\) Since \\(a\\lt b,\\) \\(x\\) is smaller. From \\(k(a+b)=c,\\) \\(k=\\frac{c}{a+b},\\) so \\(x=\\frac{ac}{a+b}.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Write the numbers as \\(ka\\) and \\(kb\\)",
        "Use their sum to determine the common scale factor"
      ],
